# AIO uppercase typography (mandatory · founder rule 2026-10-07)

Applies to **every All In One Enterprises page** — the standalone app in `all-in-one-enterprises/` (public site, client portal, office, staff, migration, activation, IFTA, every workspace and every future page).

## Rule

**ALL visible text is UPPERCASE.**

**Only exception:** password `<input>` fields keep the real case of what is typed — hidden **and** when revealed by a show/hide toggle. Every password field carries `data-aio-password` (a revealed field switches to `type="text"`). Their labels and placeholders stay uppercase.

The founder's preference **takes precedence over every design authority**: when an approved authority image, mock, storyboard or reference draws sentence case, title case or lowercase, the implementation is still UPPERCASE.

## Enforcement

- Global safety net: `all-in-one-enterprises/src/styles/aio-uppercase.css` — `text-transform: uppercase !important` on `body`, every descendant, pseudo-elements and placeholders, with the single password exemption (`input[type=password]`, `input[data-aio-password]`). It is imported **last** in `src/App.tsx`. Never remove or weaken it.
- New password inputs (and any show/hide password component) must carry `data-aio-password`.
- Browser tab titles: `src/utils/uppercaseDocumentTitle.ts` (installed in `main.tsx`) uppercases `document.title` whoever sets it.
- Text that CSS cannot reach must be authored uppercase in source: native `alert` / `confirm` / `prompt`, notifications, emails/SMS, exported files and PDFs, text baked into images, canvas text.

## When matching an authority

- Keep the authority's composition; set the copy uppercase and **fit the size** so each block keeps its line count and stays inside its panel (see the generated "UPPERCASE FIT" block in `src/client-migration/visual/aio-migration.css` and `docs/AIO_CLIENT_MIGRATION_AUTHORITY_RECOVERY.md`).
- Visual QA compares layout and fit, not letter case.

## Do not

- Add `text-transform: none | lowercase | capitalize` to any AIO text (the global rule overrides it anyway — do not leave misleading declarations in new code).
- Lowercase labels, body copy, empty states, nav items, table data or user-entered values to match a reference.
- Exempt anything other than password inputs. Email and every other typed value displays uppercase; the stored value is exactly what was typed.

